    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.surround\n\n### Description\n\nExample:\r\n\r\n> Starting position\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<p class=\"foo\">Lo*rem ipsum</p>\r\n```\r\n\r\n1. Cursor represented by asterisk\r\n2. Press `csttspan<CR>`\r\n\r\n> Current result:\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<span>Lorem ipsum</span>\r\n```\r\n\r\n> Desired result:\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<span class=\"foo\">Lorem ipsum</span>\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Prior art\r\n\r\n- vim-surround [keeps](https://github.com/tpope/vim-surround/blob/3d188ed2113431cf8dac77be61b842acb64433d9/doc/surround.txt#L132-L136) keeps the attributes. However if you end your pattern with `>` (e.g. `srttspan><CR>`), it omits them.",
