        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for suggestion!\r\n\r\nUnfortunately this is out of scope for 'mini.surround' as it doesn't really fit its design. Replacing is done uniformly for all surroundings:\r\n- First find left and right parts for input surrounding. In your case it is `<p class=\"foo\">` and `</p>`.\r\n- Replace found left and right parts with left and right parts of output surrounding correspondingly. As after `tspan<CR>` left and right parts are `<span>` and `</span>`, the result is what you are seeing.\r\n\r\nThe best suggestion I can make within 'mini.surround' functionality is to manually supply attributes for output surrounding. So type `srt` followed by `t`, `span class=\"foo\"`, and `<CR>`.",
